    "narrative": "The offensive output for Ghost Ride the WHIP hinges on a targeted assault against favorable matchups, led by **Corbin Carroll** (80.64) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91). **Corbin Carroll** is our primary anchor today; beyond the favorable 4.14 xERA of the opposing starter, his 100% success rate against the pitcher's delivery cycle offers a rare opportunity to bank elite stolen base upside. Similarly, **Tyler Soderstrom** benefits from a massive 10% park boost and a soft matchup against Ure\u00f1a, making him a high-leverage play in the three-hole. We are also leaning into **Jose Caballero** (75.83) and **Seiya Suzuki** (71.48); both are maximizing their respective platoon advantages against left-handed starters, with **Jose Caballero** specifically providing a strong 13% boost from his dynamic platoon splits that elevates him well above his base projection.\n\nThe decision to limit the starting lineup to those exceeding our efficiency floor leaves **Zach McKinstry** (41.35) as the most difficult omission. While **Zach McKinstry** graded out as a viable utility option, his projected efficiency fell narrowly behind our baseline starters due to a unfavorable matchup against a sub-3.40 xERA arm and a suboptimal spot at the bottom of the order. Meanwhile, **Cole Young** (39.73) missed the cut entirely, failing to eclipse our 40-point floor. We continue to monitor the status of **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Mickey Moniak**, both of whom remain sidelined on the IL, leaving the heavy lifting to our core group. We will look to **James Wood** to mitigate the slight disadvantage of facing a sub-4.00 xERA arm through his elite 0.402 xwOBA, while keeping a close eye on **Dalton Rushing**, whose efficiency (44.02) remains fragile due to his placement at the bottom of the order and the presence of a left-on-left platoon disadvantage.",
